  "description": "Polite outbound injection. The instruction is courteous rather than commanding, so nothing in it looks like an attack to a keyword list: an addressee aimed at the agent, an outbound action, and an external destination, each within 64 gap characters of the next in total and never across a blank line, where a line break that is not followed by a blank line counts as one gap character. This is the shape v0.5.5 allowed on every channel while it blocked the loud paraphrase of the same request (STATE #50). Known limits, measured: an attack that names no destination is deliberately not matched; an addressee written as '<agent-noun> <role-noun>:' is missed; and a human-process document that literally addresses the assistant and names an external address will fire, because that is the attack shape.",
  "keywords": [
    "polite outbound action",
    "agent-directed send",
    "assistant outbound instruction"
  ],
